===persian===

بابا مأمور شهرداری بود
پا با سنگها را میکشت
یک روز آفتابی
بابا
با یک تکه گوشت زهر آلود
در تعقیب سگی بود...
بچه گداها بازی میکردند
بچه گداها با سگ بازی میکردند
سگ گوشت را نخورد
بچه گداها خوردند.
بچه گداها مردند.
بابا دید
بابا خندید
بابا قاتل بود
با با گوشت خورد
بابا مرد...
من نصف حقوق بابا را از شهرداری میگرفتم
من درس خواندم
من شهردار شدم
من سگ ها را نمی کشم
من سگ ها را عقیم میکنم
شاید بچه گداها عقیم شوند.

نشریه نامه دانشجو دانشگاه تهران (۱۳۴۱)

===machine===

Dad was a municipal official
He used to beat stones
One sunny day
Dad
He was chasing a dog with a piece of poisoned meat...
The beggar children were playing
The beggar children were playing with the dog
The dog did not eat the meat
The beggar children did.
The beggar children died.
Dad saw
Dad laughed
Dad was a murderer
He ate the meat
Dad died...
I used to get half of Dad's salary from the municipality
I studied
I became the mayor
I do not kill dogs
I sterilize dogs
Maybe the beggar children will be sterilized.

Tehran University Student's Newsletter (1962)

===lantern===

Dad worked for the city;
he was the one who killed the dogs.
One sunny day
Dad
went out after a stray
with a scrap of poisoned meat...
The beggar children were playing,
the beggar children were playing with the dog.
The dog wouldn't eat the meat.
The beggar children ate it.
The beggar children died.
Dad saw.
Dad laughed.
Dad was a murderer.
Dad ate the meat.
Dad died...
I drew half of Dad's wages from the city.
I studied.
I became mayor.
I don't kill the dogs —
I sterilize the dogs.
Maybe the beggar children will be sterilized too.

Tehran University Student Newsletter, 1341

